Read the 2-line diff in `static/sessions.js` (PR head 9ddf36f) plus the surrounding `newSession()` / `loadSession()` / `renderMessages()` paths on origin/master. The fix is correct and matches the existing pattern at `static/sessions.js:590-591`. The PR description's diagnosis is accurate, and the symptom is real: after a `newSession()` from a session that had truncated history, the load-older indicator renders on a brand-new conversation with no actual older messages.

## Code reference

`renderMessages()` decides whether to render the "Load earlier messages" affordance from the module-level `_messagesTruncated` flag — see `static/ui.js:6298-6312`:

```js
