`newSession()` (pre-fix) only did `S.toolCalls=[]` and then later `S.session=data.session; S.messages=data.session.messages||[]` at `static/sessions.js:490`. It never touched the module-level `_messagesTruncated` or `_oldestIdx`. The server returns `_messages_truncated: false` for a fresh session, but `S.session=data.session` doesn't lift that into the module flag — that lift only happens in `_ensureMessagesLoaded()` at line 1304, which `newSession()` doesn't call. So whatever the previous session left behind survives the transition.

## Diagnosis

The patch resets both module flags inside the `_newSessionInFlight` IIFE adjacent to the `S.toolCalls=[]` clear:

```js
_newSessionInFlight=(async()=>{
  updateQueueBadge();
  S.toolCalls=[];
  _messagesTruncated=false;
  _oldestIdx=0;
  clearLiveToolCards();
```

That's the right placement — it happens before the `/api/session/new` POST so any error in the request still leaves the flags in a clean state, and it mirrors `loadSession()`'s reset block. CI is green on 3.11/3.12/3.13. No tests need to change because there's no Python-side behavior here.

